   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>.
   .... The relation holds.

 .. Else if let `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `externMethodTypeIR`:
  ... Check that `routineTypeIR'` has type `externMethodTypeIR`.
  ... Let `externMethodTypeIR'` be `routineTypeIR'`.
  ... Check that `externMethodTypeIR'` matches pattern `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( % ) -> %`.
  ... Let `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `externMethodTypeIR'`.
  ... Group externmethod-abstract: `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` and `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~`

   .... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for each `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>.
   .... The relation holds.

. Else if let `PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `routineTypeIR'` has type `parserApplyMethodTypeIR`.
 .. Let `PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR'`.
 .. Group parserapply: `PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` and `PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )`

  ... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for each `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `routineTypeIR'` has type `controlApplyMethodTypeIR`.
 .. Let `CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR'`.
 .. Group controlapply: `CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` and `CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )`

  ... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for each `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `TABLE_APPLY -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `routineTypeIR'` has type `tableApplyMethodTypeIR`.
 .. Let `TABLE_APPLY -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `routineTypeIR'`.
 .. Group tableapply: `TABLE_APPLY -> typeIR~ret_a~` and `TABLE_APPLY -> typeIR~ret_b~`

  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.

relation RoutineTypeDef_alpha: `routineTypeDefIR` and `routineTypeDefIR'`

. If let `routineTypeIR~a~` be `routineTypeDefIR`:
 .. Check that `routineTypeDefIR'` has type `routineTypeIR`.
 .. Let `routineTypeIR~b~` be `routineTypeDefIR'`.
 .. Group mono: `routineTypeIR~a~` and `routineTypeIR~b~`

  ... Check that <<RoutineType_alpha, `routineTypeIR~a~` and `routineTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `routineTypeIR~a~ < tid~a~^{asterisk}^ , tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `routineTypeDefIR`:
 .. Check that `routineTypeDefIR'` has type `polyRoutineTypeDefIR`.
 .. Let `routineTypeIR~b~ < tid~b~^{asterisk}^ , tid~hidden_b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `routineTypeDefIR'`.
 .. Group poly: `routineTypeIR~a~ < tid~a~^{asterisk}^ , tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^ >` and `routineTypeIR~b~ < tid~b~^{asterisk}^ , tid~hidden_b~^{asterisk}^ >`

  ... Check that the length of `tid~a~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `tid~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that the length of `tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `tid~hidden_b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be <<fresh_tids, `the length of tid~a~^{asterisk}^ + the length of tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^` fresh type variables>>.
  ... Let `tid~a'~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~a~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `theta~a~` be `{ tid~a'~ : TID tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `routineTypeIR~a_subst~` be `$subst_routineType(theta~a~, routineTypeIR~a~)`.
  ... Let `tid~b'~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~b~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~hidden_b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `theta~b~` be `{ tid~b'~ : TID tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `routineTypeIR~b_subst~` be `$subst_routineType(theta~b~, routineTypeIR~b~)`.
  ... Check that <<RoutineType_alpha, `routineTypeIR~a_subst~` and `routineTypeIR~b_subst~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.

relation Type_wf: `bound` and `typeIR'''`

. If let `baseTypeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group baseTypeIR: `bound` and `baseTypeIR`

  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `TID tid` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group nameTypeIR: `bound` and `TID tid`

  ... Check that `$in_set<tid>(tid, bound)`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `polyTypeDefIR < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group specializedTypeIR: `bound` and `polyTypeDefIR < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >`

  ... Let `typeIR` be `$specialize_typeDef(polyTypeDefIR, typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `TYPEDEF _ typeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group typedefTypeIR: `bound` and `TYPEDEF _ typeIR`

  ... Check that <<nestable_typedef, `typeIR` can be used in a typedef>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `TYPE _ typeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group newTypeIR: `bound` and `TYPE _ typeIR`

  ... Check that <<nestable_new, `typeIR` can be used in a new type>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `LIST < typeIR >` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group listTypeIR: `bound` and `LIST < typeIR >`

  ... Check that <<nestable_list, `typeIR` can be nested in a list type>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `TUPLE < typeIR^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group tupleTypeIR: `bound` and `TUPLE < typeIR^{asterisk}^ >`

  ... Check that <<nestable_tuple, `typeIR` can be nested in a tuple type>>, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `typeIR [ _ ]` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group headerStackTypeIR: `bound` and `typeIR [ _ ]`

  ... Check that <<nestable_headerStack, `typeIR` can be nested in a header stack type>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `STRUCT _ { typeIR id ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group structTypeIR: `bound` and `STRUCT _ { typeIR id ;^{asterisk}^ }`

  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
  ... Check that <<nestable_struct, `typeIR` can be nested in a struct type>>, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `HEADER _ { typeIR id ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group headerTypeIR: `bound` and `HEADER _ { typeIR id ;^{asterisk}^ }`

  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
  ... Check that <<nestable_header, `typeIR` can be used in a header type>>, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `HEADER_UNION _ { typeIR id ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group headerUnionTypeIR: `bound` and `HEADER_UNION _ { typeIR id ;^{asterisk}^ }`

  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
  ... Check that <<nestable_headerUnion, `typeIR` can be used in a header union type>>, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. If let `ENUM _ { id^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
  ... Group enumTypeIR-non-serializable: `bound` and `ENUM _ { id^{asterisk}^ }`

   .... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
   .... The relation holds.

 .. Else if let `ENUM _ # typeIR { id = _ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
  ... Group enumTypeIR-serializable: `bound` and `ENUM _ # typeIR { id = _ ;^{asterisk}^ }`

   .... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
   .... Check that <<nestable_enum_serializable, `typeIR` can be used in a serializable enum type>>.
