relation Argument_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `argument`

. Check that `argument` has type `expression`.
. Let `expression` be `argument`.
. Group expression: `p`, `TC`, and `expression`

 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Result in the typed argument `typedExpressionIR`.
. If let `name = expression` be `argument`:
 .. Group name-expression: `p`, `TC`, and `name = expression`

  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the typed argument `nameIR = typedExpressionIR`.

. Else if let `name = _` be `argument`:
 .. Group name-dontcare: `p`, `TC`, and `name = _`

  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Result in the typed argument `nameIR = _`.

. Else if `argument` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare: `p`, `TC`, and `_`

  ... Result in the typed argument `_`.

relation Lvalue_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `lvalue`

. Check that `lvalue` has type `prefixedNonTypeName`.
. Let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `lvalue`.
. Group referenceExpression-prefixedNonTypeName: `p`, `TC`, and `prefixedNonTypeName`

 .. Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
