relation Decls_ok: `p`, `TC'`, and `declaration^{asterisk}^`

. If `declaration^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `p`, `TC'`, and `[ ]`

  ... Result in the modified typing context `TC'` and the typed declarations `[ ]`.

. Else if let `declaration~h~ :: declaration~t~^{asterisk}^` be `declaration^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `p`, `TC'`, and `declaration~h~ :: declaration~t~^{asterisk}^`

  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR~h~` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `declaration~h~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC'`,
        * and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Decls_ok, typing `declaration~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC~1~`,
        * and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Result in the modified typing context `TC~2~` and the typed declarations `declarationIR~h~ :: declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Program_ok: `p4program`

. Group : `p4program`

 .. Let `declaration^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_p4program, the list of declarations in `p4program`>>.
 .. Let `TC~0~` be `$empty_typingContext`.
 .. Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Decls_ok, typing `declaration^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `GLOBAL` and typing context `TC~0~`,
      * and the modified typing context>>.
 .. Result in the typing context `TC~1~` and the typed P4 program `declarationIR^{asterisk}^ ;`.

relation Call_convention_expr_ok: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `direction typeIR~param~ _ _^?^`, and `typedExpressionIR~arg~`

. If `direction` matches pattern `IN`:
 .. Group in: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `IN typeIR~param~ _ _^?^`, and `typedExpressionIR~arg~`

  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`  to  `typeIR~param~`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~`.
. Group out-inout: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `direction typeIR~param~ _ _^?^`, and `typedExpressionIR~arg~`

 .. If let `typeIR~arg~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~param~` and `typeIR~arg~` are the same type>>.
  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~arg~`>> holds.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg~`.

 .. Else if let `typeIR~arg~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~param~` and `typeIR~arg~` are the same type>>.
  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~arg~`>> holds.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg~`.
. If `direction` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
 .. Group empty: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `typeIR~param~ _ _^?^`, and `typedExpressionIR~arg~`

  ... If let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`  to  `typeIR~param~`>>:
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
   .... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~`.

  ... Else if let `typeIR~arg~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>:
   .... Let `ctk~arg~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
