. Else if let `parameterTypeIR~h~ :: parameterTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `_ :: _`.
 .. Let `argumentIR~h~ :: argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group cons: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR~h~ :: parameterTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~h~ :: argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^`

  ... Let `argumentIR~h_cast~` be the result of <<Call_convention_argument_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR~h~` applied to parameter type `parameterTypeIR~h~`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `actctxt`>>.
  ... Let `argumentIR~t_cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `actctxt`>>.
  ... Result in `argumentIR~h_cast~ :: argumentIR~t_cast~^{asterisk}^`.

relation RoutineTarget_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `routineTarget`

. Group referenceExpression: `p`, `TC`, and `routineTarget`

 .. If `routineTarget` has type `prefixedNonTypeName`:
  ... Let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `routineTarget`.
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
  ... Check that `prefixedNameIR = ` "verify" \/ prefixedNameIR = . "verify" => p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND) \/ p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)`.
  ... Result in the typed routine target `prefixedNameIR`.
 .. If `routineTarget` is equal to `THIS`:
  ... Result in the typed routine target `` "this"`.
. If let `memberAccessBase . member` be `routineTarget`:
 .. Group memberAccessExpression: `p`, `TC`, and `memberAccessBase . member`

  ... If let `prefixedTypeName` be `memberAccessBase`:
   .... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Result in the typed routine target `TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR`.

  ... Else if let `expression~base~` be `memberAccessBase`:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Result in the typed routine target `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR`.

. Else if let `( expression )` be `routineTarget`:
 .. Group parenthesizedExpression: `p`, `TC`, and `( expression )`

  ... Let `routineTargetIR` be the result of <<RoutineTarget_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the typed routine target `( routineTargetIR )`.

relation RoutineTarget_lvalue_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `lvalue`

. Group : `p`, `TC`, and `lvalue`

