  ... Result in `typeIR~ret_inferred~`, `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.

. Else if let `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
 .. Check that `tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
 .. Group action: `p`, `TC`, `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )`, `[ ]`, `[ ]`, `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default'~^{asterisk}^`

  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `$filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)`.
