 .. Let `(constructorTypeIR, tid~impl~^{asterisk}^)` be `$specialize_constructorTypeDef(constructorTypeDefIR, typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^)`.
 .. Let `bound` be <<union_set, the union of the sets `$bound(p, TC)` and `{ tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
 .. Check that <<ConstructorType_wf, `bound |- constructorTypeIR`>> holds.
 .. Result in `constructorTypeIR`, `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Inst_ok: `cursor'`, `TC`, `instctxt`, `constructorTypeIR`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^`, `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`

. Check that `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`.
. Group package: `GLOBAL`, `TC`, `instctxt`, `constructorTypeIR`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^`, `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`

 .. Let `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~object~` be `constructorTypeIR`.
