relation Decl_object_ok: `p`, `TC~0~`, `typeFrame`, `rdenv`, and `objectDeclaration`

. If let `annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement` be `objectDeclaration`:
 .. Group functionDeclaration: `p`, `TC~0~`, `typeFrame`, `rdenv`, and `annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement`

  ... Let `TC~1~` be `TC~0~`[BLOCK.KIND = `EXTERN`].
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `TC~1~`[BLOCK.FRAME = `typeFrame`].
  ... Let `typeParameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeParameterListOpt, the list of type parameters in `typeParameterListOpt`>>.
  ... Let `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~expl~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~expl~` be <<name, the name of `typeParameter`>>
--
+
for each `typeParameter` in `typeParameter^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `$add_types(LOCAL, TC~2~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, TID tid~expl~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `typeIR~ret~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `typeOrVoid`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~3~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parameterList, the list of parameters in `parameterList`>>.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~3~`>>.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_parameterIR, the type of  `parameterIR`>>
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~4~` be `$add_parameters(LOCAL, TC~3~, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `TC~5~` be `TC~4~`[LOCAL.KIND = `EXTERN_METHOD -> typeIR~ret~`].
  ... Let `_`, `f`, and `blockStatementIR` be the result of <<Block_ok, typing `blockStatement`, under typing context `TC~5~` and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... If `f` matches pattern `RET`:
   .... Let `rid` be `$rid(name, parameterList)`.
   .... Let `methodTypeIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
   .... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `methodTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
   .... Check that <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `$bound(p, TC~0~) |- routineTypeDefIR`>> holds.
   .... Let `rdenv~init~` be `$update_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `functionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR`.
   .... Result in `typeFrame`, `rdenv~init~`, and `functionDeclarationIR`.
  ... If `typeIR~ret~` is equal to `VOID`:
   .... Let `rid` be `$rid(name, parameterList)`.
   .... Let `methodTypeIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
   .... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `methodTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
   .... Check that <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `$bound(p, TC~0~) |- routineTypeDefIR`>> holds.
   .... Let `rdenv~init~` be `$update_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `functionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR`.
   .... Result in `typeFrame`, `rdenv~init~`, and `functionDeclarationIR`.

. Else if let `instantiation` be `objectDeclaration`:
 .. Group instantiation: `p`, `TC~0~`, `typeFrame`, `rdenv`, and `instantiation`

  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `instantiation`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC~0~`,
        * and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `instantiationIR`.
  ... Let `instantiationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Let `_ _ _ < _ > ( _ ) nameIR _ ;` be `instantiationIR`.
  ... Let `varTypeIR'^?^` be `$find_var(p, TC~1~, ` nameIR)`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?varTypeIR` be `varTypeIR'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeFrame~init~` be `$update_map<id, varTypeIR>(typeFrame, nameIR, varTypeIR)`.
  ... Result in `typeFrame~init~`, `rdenv`, and `instantiationIR`.

relation Decls_object_ok: `p`, `TC`, `typeFrame'`, `rdenv'`, and `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^`

. If `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `p`, `TC`, `typeFrame'`, `rdenv'`, and `[ ]`

  ... Result in `typeFrame'`, `rdenv'`, and `[ ]`.

. Else if let `objectDeclaration~h~ :: objectDeclaration~t~^{asterisk}^` be `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `p`, `TC`, `typeFrame'`, `rdenv'`, and `objectDeclaration~h~ :: objectDeclaration~t~^{asterisk}^`

  ... <<Decl_object_ok, `p TC typeFrame' rdenv' |- objectDeclaration~h~ : typeFrame~1~ rdenv~1~ objectDeclarationIR~h~`>>.
  ... <<Decls_object_ok, `p TC typeFrame~1~ rdenv~1~ |- objectDeclaration~t~^{asterisk}^ : typeFrame~2~ rdenv~2~ objectDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `typeFrame~2~`, `rdenv~2~`, and `objectDeclarationIR~h~ :: objectDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Enum_serializable_field_ok: `TC~0~`, `nameIR~enum~`, `typeIR`, and `name = expression`

. Group : `TC~0~`, `nameIR~enum~`, `typeIR`, and `name = expression`

 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR`  to  `typeIR`>>.
 .. Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
 .. Let `?typedExpressionIR~cast~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
 .. Check that `<<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  typedExpressionIR~cast~>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
 .. Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~cast~`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
 .. Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR~enum~` be `ENUM nameIR~enum~ # typeIR { [ ] }`.
 .. Let `value~enum~` be `nameIR~enum~ . nameIR # value`.
 .. Let `TC~1~` be `$add_var(BLOCK, TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~enum~ LCTK ?value~enum~)`.
 .. Result in `TC~1~`, `nameIR = typedExpressionIR~cast~`, and `value`.

relation Enum_serializable_fields_ok: `TC'`, `nameIR~enum~`, `typeIR`, and `namedExpression^{asterisk}^`

. If `namedExpression^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `TC'`, `nameIR~enum~`, `typeIR`, and `[ ]`

  ... Result in `TC'`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.

. Else if let `namedExpression~h~ :: namedExpression~t~^{asterisk}^` be `namedExpression^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `TC'`, `nameIR~enum~`, `typeIR`, and `namedExpression~h~ :: namedExpression~t~^{asterisk}^`

  ... <<Enum_serializable_field_ok, `TC' nameIR~enum~ typeIR |- namedExpression~h~ : TC~1~ namedExpressionIR~h~ # value~field_h~`>>.
  ... <<Enum_serializable_fields_ok, `TC~1~ nameIR~enum~ typeIR |- namedExpression~t~^{asterisk}^ : TC~2~ namedExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^ # value~field_t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Let `namedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^` be `namedExpressionIR~h~ :: namedExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `value~field~^{asterisk}^` be `value~field_h~ :: value~field_t~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Result in `TC~2~`, `namedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`, and `value~field~^{asterisk}^`.

relation SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `TC`, `typeIR~key~`, and `simpleKeysetExpression`

. Check that `simpleKeysetExpression` has type `expression`.
. Let `expression` be `simpleKeysetExpression`.
. Group expression-set-alpha: `TC`, `typeIR~key~`, and `expression`

 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR''` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Check that `typeIR''` has type `setTypeIR`.
 .. Let `SET < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''`.
 .. Check that `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[ _/1 ]`.
 .. Let `[typeIR]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR` and `typeIR~key~` are the same type>>.
 .. Result in `typedExpressionIR`.
. Group expression-set-subtype: `TC`, `typeIR~key~`, and `expression`

 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR''` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Check that `typeIR''` has type `setTypeIR`.
 .. Let `SET < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''`.
 .. Check that `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[ _/1 ]`.
 .. Let `[typeIR]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR` and `typeIR~key~` are not the same type>>.
 .. Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR~cast~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be `( typeIR~cast~ ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR~cast~ DYN )`.
 .. Result in `typedExpressionIR~cast~`.
. Group expression-non-set: `TC`, `typeIR~key~`, and `expression`

 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Check that `$is_set_typeIR(typeIR)`.
 .. Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR~cast~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be `( typeIR~cast~ ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR~cast~ DYN )`.
 .. Result in `typedExpressionIR~cast~`.
. If let `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group mask: `TC`, `typeIR~key~`, and `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~`

  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_mask)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~ &&& typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~`.

. Else if let `expression~l~ .. expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group range: `TC`, `typeIR~key~`, and `expression~l~ .. expression~r~`

  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_range)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Check that `typeIR~reduced~` is equal to <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~ .. typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~`.

. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `DEFAULT`:
 .. Group default: `TC`, `typeIR~key~`, and `DEFAULT`

  ... Result in `DEFAULT`.

. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare: `TC`, `typeIR~key~`, and `_`

  ... Result in `_`.

relation SelectCase_keyset_ok: `TC`, `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`, and `keysetExpression`

. Check that `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[ _/1 ]`.
. Let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
. If let `expression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-expression: `TC`, `[typeIR~key~]`, and `expression`

  ... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.

. Else if let `tupleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. If let `( expression~l~ &&& expression~r~ )` be `tupleKeysetExpression`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-mask: `TC`, `[typeIR~key~]`, and `( expression~l~ &&& expression~r~ )`

   .... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ &&& expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.

 .. Else if let `( expression~l~ .. expression~r~ )` be `tupleKeysetExpression`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-range: `TC`, `[typeIR~key~]`, and `( expression~l~ .. expression~r~ )`

   .... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ .. expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
. Check that `keysetExpression` has type `simpleKeysetExpression`.
. Let `simpleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`.
. If let `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-mask: `TC`, `[typeIR~key~]`, and `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~`

  ... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ &&& expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.

. Else if let `expression~l~ .. expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-range: `TC`, `[typeIR~key~]`, and `expression~l~ .. expression~r~`

  ... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ .. expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
. If let `simpleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. If `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `DEFAULT`:
  ... Group simpleKeysetExpression-default: `TC`, `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`, and `DEFAULT`

   .... If `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`:
    ..... Result in `DEFAULT`.
   .... Let `typeIR''^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... If `typeIR''^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[ _/1 ]`:
    ..... Let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR''^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
   .... If the length of `typeIR''^{asterisk}^` is greater than 1:
    ..... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR''^{asterisk}^ > |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.

 .. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `_`:
  ... Group simpleKeysetExpression-dontcare: `TC`, `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`, and `_`

   .... Let `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... If `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[ _/1 ]`:
    ..... Let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
   .... If the length of `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is greater than 1:
    ..... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ > |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.

. Else if let `tupleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. If `tupleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `( DEFAULT )`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-default: `TC`, `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`, and `( DEFAULT )`

   .... Let `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... If `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[ _/1 ]`:
    ..... Let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
   .... If the length of `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is greater than 1:
    ..... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ > |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.

 .. Else if `tupleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `( _ )`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-dontcare: `TC`, `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`, and `( _ )`

   .... Let `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... If `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[ _/1 ]`:
    ..... Let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
   .... If the length of `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is greater than 1:
    ..... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ > |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.

 .. Else if let `( simpleKeysetExpression~h~ , simpleKeysetExpressionList~t~ )` be `tupleKeysetExpression`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-list: `TC`, `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`, and `( simpleKeysetExpression~h~ , simpleKeysetExpressionList~t~ )`

   .... Let `simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_simpleKeysetExpressionList, the list of simple keyset expressions in `simpleKeysetExpressionList~t~`>>.
   .... Let `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^` be `simpleKeysetExpression~h~ :: simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that the length of `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^`.
   .... <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR''' |- simpleKeysetExpression : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>, for each `simpleKeysetExpression` in `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^`, `simpleKeysetExpressionIR` in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`, and `typeIR'''` in `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Result in `( simpleKeysetExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ )`.

relation SelectCase_ok: `TC`, `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`, `typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^`, and `keysetExpression : name ;`

. Group : `TC`, `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`, `typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^`, and `keysetExpression : name ;`

 .. <<SelectCase_keyset_ok, `TC typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^ |- keysetExpression : keysetExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
 .. Check that `nameIR` is in `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Result in `keysetExpressionIR : nameIR ;`.

relation TableEntry_keyset_simple_ok: `TC`, `TBLC`, (`typeIR~key~`, `text`), and `simpleKeysetExpression`

. If `simpleKeysetExpression` has type `expression`:
 .. Let `expression` be `simpleKeysetExpression`.
 .. Group expression: `TC`, `TBLC`, (`typeIR~key~`, `text`), and `expression`

  ... If `text` = "lpm":
   .... Let `matchMode` be `TBLC.MODE`.
   .... Check that `matchMode` matches pattern `NOPRILPM %`.
   .... Let `NOPRILPM n` be `matchMode`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Let `ctk` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~set~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~set~` be `( typeIR~set~ ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR~set~ ctk )`.
   .... Result in `LPM n` and `typedExpressionIR~set~`.

  ... Else if `text` =/= "lpm":
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Let `ctk` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~set~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~set~` be `( typeIR~set~ ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR~set~ ctk )`.
   .... Result in `NOLPM` and `typedExpressionIR~set~`.
. If let `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group mask: `TC`, `TBLC`, (`typeIR~key~`, `text`), and `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~`

  ... If `text` = "lpm":
   .... Let `matchMode` be `TBLC.MODE`.
   .... Check that `matchMode` matches pattern `NOPRILPM %`.
   .... Let `NOPRILPM n` be `matchMode`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
   .... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_mask)`.
   .... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
   .... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~reduced~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
   .... Check that `ctk~r_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
   .... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `i~r~` be `$to_number(value~r~)`.
   .... Let `n~prefix~` be `$tableEntry_lpm_prefix(n W $to_bitstr(n, i~r~))`.
   .... Result in `LPM n~prefix~` and `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ &&& typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`.

  ... Else if `text` = "ternary":
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
   .... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_mask)`.
