  ... Result in `TBLS~3~` and `simpleKeysetExpressionIR~h~ :: simpleKeysetExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Expr_lvalue_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `expressionIR # ( _ _ )`

. If let `prefixedNameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group referenceExpressionIR: `p`, `TC`, and `prefixedNameIR # ( _ _ )`

  ... Let `varTypeIR^?^` be `$find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?direction _ ctk _^?^` be `varTypeIR^?^`.
  ... Check that `ctk` matches pattern `DYN`.
  ... If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
   .... The relation holds.

  ... Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
   .... The relation holds.

. Else if let `memberAccessBaseIR . nameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Check that `memberAccessBaseIR` has type `typedExpressionIR`.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be `memberAccessBaseIR`.
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-memberAccessExpressionIR: `p`, `TC`, and `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR # ( _ _ )`

  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>> holds.
  ... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... If `typeIR'` has type `headerStackTypeIR`:
   .... Let `typeIR [ _ ]` be `typeIR'`.
   .... If `nameIR` = "next":
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)`:
     ...... The relation holds.
    ..... If `p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)`:
     ...... The relation holds.

   .... Else if `nameIR` = "last":
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)`:
     ...... The relation holds.
    ..... If `p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)`:
     ...... The relation holds.
  ... If `$is_headerStackTypeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR~base~>>)`:
   .... The relation holds.

. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index~ ]` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-indexAccessExpressionIR: `p`, `TC`, and `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index~ ] # ( _ _ )`

  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ]` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-indexAccessExpressionIR-bitslice: `p`, `TC`, and `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ] # ( _ _ )`

  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

relation Expr_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `expressionIR # _`

. If let `booleanLiteral` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-boolean: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `booleanLiteral # _`

  ... If `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `TRUE`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `B true`.

  ... Else if `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `FALSE`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `B false`.

. Else if let `numberLiteral` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-number: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `numberLiteral # _`

  ... If let `D i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `D i`.

  ... Else if let `n W i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `n W i`.

  ... Else if let `n S i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `n S i`.

. Else if let `" text "` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-stringLiteral: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `" text " # _`

  ... Result in `STO'` and `" text "`.

. Else if let `prefixedNameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group referenceExpressionIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `prefixedNameIR # _`

  ... Let `value` be `$find_value_inst(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)`.
  ... Result in `STO'` and `value`.

. Else if let `defaultExpression` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group defaultExpressionIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `... # _`

  ... Result in `STO'` and `DEFAULT`.

. Else if let `unop typedExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group unaryExpressionIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `unop typedExpressionIR # _`

  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `<<un_op, unop value>>`.
. Let `( _ _ )` be `_`.
. If let `typedExpressionIR~l~ binop' typedExpressionIR~r~` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group binaryExpressionIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `typedExpressionIR~l~ binop' typedExpressionIR~r~ # ( _ _ )`

  ... Check that `binop'` is not in `[&&, ||]`.
  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~l~ ==> STO~1~ value~l~`>>.
  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~r~ ==> STO~2~ value~r~`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~2~` and `<<bin_op, value~l~ binop' value~r~>>`.
  ... If `binop'` matches pattern `&&`:
   .... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~l~ ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
   .... If `value` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... Result in `STO~1~` and `B false`.
   .... If `value` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~r~ ==> STO~2~ value~r~`>>.
    ..... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~r~`.

  ... Else if `binop'` matches pattern `||`:
   .... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~l~ ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
   .... If `value` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... Result in `STO~1~` and `B true`.
   .... If `value` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~r~ ==> STO~2~ value~r~`>>.
    ..... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~r~`.

. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~cond~ ? typedExpressionIR~true~ : typedExpressionIR~false~` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group ternaryExpressionIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `typedExpressionIR~cond~ ? typedExpressionIR~true~ : typedExpressionIR~false~ # _`

  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~cond~ ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... If `value` is equal to `B true`:
   .... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~true~ ==> STO~2~ value~true~`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~true~`.
  ... If `value` is equal to `B false`:
   .... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~false~ ==> STO~2~ value~false~`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~false~`.

. Else if let `( typeIR ) typedExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group castExpressionIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `( typeIR ) typedExpressionIR # _`

  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Let `value~cast~` be `$cast_op(typeIR, value)`.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `value~cast~`.

. Else if let `dataExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Check that `dataExpressionIR` matches pattern `{#}`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-invalid: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `{#} # _`

  ... Result in `STO'` and `{#}`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-sequence: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `dataExpressionIR # _`

  ... If let `SEQ { typedExpressionListIR }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionListIR ==> STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `SEQ ( value^{asterisk}^ )`.

  ... Else if let `SEQ { typedExpressionListIR , ... }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionListIR ==> STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `SEQ ( value^{asterisk}^ , ... )`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-record: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `dataExpressionIR # _`

  ... If let `RECORD { nameIR = typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ ==> STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `RECORD { value nameIR ;^{asterisk}^ }`.

  ... Else if let `RECORD { nameIR = typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ , ... }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ ==> STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `RECORD { value nameIR ;^{asterisk}^ , ... }`.

. Else if let `ERROR . nameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group errorAccessExpressionIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `ERROR . nameIR # _`

  ... Let `nameIR~error~` be `"error." ++ nameIR`.
  ... Let `value~error~` be `$find_value_inst(p, IC, ` nameIR~error~)`.
